Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog** audit for your integration test suite.

---

## Summary Dashboard

```
┌──────────┬─────────────┬────────────────┐
│ Severity │ Smell Count │ Affected Tests │
├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┤
│ High     │ 2           │ 2              │
│ Medium   │ 2           │ 2              │
│ Low      │ 0           │ 0              │
│ Total    │ 4           │ 4              │
└──────────┴─────────────┴────────────────┘
```

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10 · Class tagged `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

**Integration calibration applied:** Sleepy Test downgraded from High → Medium per integration-test norms. Mystery Guest & Eager Test checks adjusted (neither triggered).

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 93–109)

The `if`/`else` branch means only one assertion path ever executes per run. If `loaded` is never a `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate assertion is dead code — a hidden testing gap.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — branching changes which assertion runs
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two focused tests — one that inserts a standard user and asserts standard properties, one that inserts a `PremiumUser` and asserts the discount rate:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetStandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetPremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vera", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is never tested — bugs hide silently.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

This test inserts 100 users but never asserts anything. MSTest reports it as passing as long as no exception is thrown — so a silently corrupted insert would go undetected.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion, false confidence
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Silent data corruption — 100% false-pass rate on insert failures that don't throw.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (lines 82–89)

`Thread.Sleep(3000)` introduces a 3-second hard wait. This is non-deterministic (may be too short on slow CI, always too long otherwise) and bloats suite runtime.

> *Integration calibration: downgraded from High → Medium because async coordination delays are more tolerable in integration tests. Still a smell.*

```csharp
// ❌ Current — hard sleep, non-deterministic
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout using a retry loop or a framework-level waiter:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures on slow machines; 3s wasted on every run even when the event fires in 50ms.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

Four assertions with no explanatory messages. When one fails in CI, the stack trace shows a line number but no context about *what* was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — which assertion failed and why?
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add message parameters:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip unchanged.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip unchanged.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Database should assign a positive ID.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis in CI — developers must open the source to identify which property failed.

---

## Smells Scanned — No Findings (15 of 19 clean)

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| **Mystery Guest** | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite (`Data Source=:memory:`) — hermetic, no external deps |
| **Eager Test** | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods; integration calibration also applies |
| **Magic Number Test** | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions are self-documenting (items just inserted) |
| **Sensitive Equality** | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| **Exception Handling** | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| **General Fixture** | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` used by all 8 tests |
| **Ignored/Disabled Test** | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` attributes |
| **Duplicate Assert** | ✅ Clean | No repeated identical assertions |
| **Lazy Test** | ✅ Clean | Each test targets a distinct behavior |
| **Constructor Initialization** | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| **Default Test** | ✅ Clean | Class name is descriptive |
| **Redundant Print** | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` statements |
| **Redundant Assertion** | ✅ Clean | No tautological asserts |
| **Resource Optimism** | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite is always available |
| **Empty Test** | ✅ Clean | All methods contain executable statements |

---

## Well-Written Patterns Worth Highlighting

- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** — clean arrange/act/assert, single concern, single assertion on the outcome.
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — correctly tests concurrency with `Task.WhenAll` and asserts the final state.
- **Setup/Cleanup lifecycle** — proper use of `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` with in-memory SQLite avoids cross-test contamination.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
